From: Kernel porting effort <hunganh.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mfd: mt6358: Fix the AUD and MISC top level interrupt offsets

The MT6358 aggregates its interrupt sources into nine top level groups,
whose pending state is reported by one bit each in TOP_INT_STATUS0:

  BUCK=0 LDO=1 PSC=2 SCK=3 BM=4 HK=5 XPP=6 AUD=7 MISC=8

enum mt6358_irq_top_status_shift is missing the XPP group, so AUD is
described as bit 6 and MISC as bit 7, i.e. both are off by one.

As a consequence mt6358_irq_handler() decodes TOP_INT_STATUS0 wrongly for
those two groups: an asserted AUD group (bit 7) makes it read and
acknowledge the MISC status registers instead, an asserted XPP group
(bit 6) makes it read the AUD ones, and the real MISC group (bit 8) is
never looked at at all. Since the parent interrupt is level triggered,
any of these leaves the interrupt asserted and retriggering forever.

The two sibling PMICs already get this right: mt6357_irq_top_status_shift
lists MT6357_XPP_TOP between HK and AUD, and mt6359_irq_top_status_shift
skips bit 6 by assigning MT6359_AUD_TOP = 7 explicitly. The vendor
driver uses the same numbering for the MT6358.

Add the missing MT6358_XPP_TOP so that AUD and MISC land on bits 7 and 8.

Fixes: 4cfc2ca2a5c7 ("mfd: Add support for the MediaTek MT6358 PMIC")
Signed-off-by: Kernel porting effort <hunganh.dev@gmail.com>
---
 include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/mt6358/core.h
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ enum mt6358_irq_top_status_shift {
 	MT6358_SCK_TOP,
 	MT6358_BM_TOP,
 	MT6358_HK_TOP,
+	MT6358_XPP_TOP,
 	MT6358_AUD_TOP,
 	MT6358_MISC_TOP,
 };
